    Presenter: no prime hold on SteamVR (V439)
    
    V438 held every presenter prime for one presenter frame, so that a reset
    in a cheap scene could not burst. SteamVR is the one runtime whose
    presenter frames do not come at a steady cadence: the layer steers their
    phase itself and jumps a whole scanout when the reading goes far,
    SteamVR's xrEndFrame blocks while the GPU is behind, and SteamVR drops
    the application to half rate when it judges its frames late. A hold
    counted in those frames is not the one-period hold it is elsewhere.
    
    MSFS 2024 in 3X at 90 Hz primes several times a second on SteamVR. On
    0.2.13.1 it ran 16-19 game frames a second on an RX 9070 XT, with
    SteamVR's half-rate flag on 62-83% of frames, against 30 on V430 in the
    same flight; issue 21 (RTX 5090) delivered a median 63 for a presenter
    submitting 90. In both, SteamVR's xrEndFrame blocked over 15 ms several
    times a second, mostly within 40 ms of a prime (85% on issue 21), never
    after a phase jump. No SteamVR or Pimax OpenXR log from V427 to V437
    shows the burst cycle the hold fixes: 0 failed end-frame captures in
    about 90,000.
    
    presenter_holds_primes is false on SteamVR and gates both hold sites,
    after the hand-over and at the D3D11/Vulkan admission hold. A SteamVR
    prime is released as soon as it is handed over, as in V437; every other
    runtime keeps V438's hold.
    
    ctest 86/86; the pipelined, 3X SteamVR presenter, 3X flight-simulator
    and own-display-time scenarios looped eight times each. Not yet run in
    a headset.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

